            <ArticleTitle>Turn up the heat: circulating serotonin tunes our internal heating system.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>156-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2015.01.011</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1550-4131(15)00012-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Serotonin acts as neurotransmitter in the brain and as a multifaceted signaling molecule coordinating many physiological processes in the periphery. In a recent issue of Nature Medicine, Crane et al. (2014) find that peripheral serotonin controls thermogenesis in adipose tissue by modulating β-adrenergic stimulation of UCP-1, thereby affecting glucose homeostasis and weight gain.</AbstractText>
